    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Siam’s kingdom under the Chakri dynasty, ruled from Bangkok, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rama-i">Rama I</a> founded in 1782 after deposing Taksin.</li><li>It dominated the Lao states, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cambodia">Cambodia</a> and the northern Malay sultanates before European pressure forced cessions.</li><li>Mongkut and Chulalongkorn modernised the state and kept Siam independent until the 1932 revolution ended absolute rule.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Mongkut spent 27 years as a Buddhist monk before becoming king in 1851, founding the reformist Thammayut order and studying Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#babylonian-astronomy">astronomy</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

